, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEiCMQBEG5IWvKriqkDFQgBFQAAAAAYASUAAMhCPQCAokN4AQ==&rs=AOn4CLB651JAGwrZIvETRmrfnjdhgqWLew", "height": 110, "width": 196, "preference": -7, "id": "31", "resolution": "196x110"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCPYBEIoBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLA3WXiluUMhFeUNNMtazX4s_e8Gdw", "height": 138, "width": 246, "preference": -7, "id": "32", "resolution": "246x138"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCNACELwBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLCJA2B4iniSI3XijFKifkL0OMSsfA", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "33", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.jpg", "height": 360, "width": 480, "preference": -7, "id": "34", "resolution": "480x360"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.webp", "preference": -6, "id": "35"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/sddefault.jpg", "preference": -5, "id": "36"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/2XvHkO3kjHE/sddefault.webp", "preference": -4, "id": "37"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hq720.jpg", "preference": -3, "id": "38"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/2XvHkO3kjHE/hq720.webp", "preference": -2, "id": "39"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/maxresdefault.jpg", "preference": -1, "id": "40"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/2XvHkO3kjHE/maxresdefault.webp", "preference": 0, "id": "41"}], "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2XvHkO3kjHE/hqdefault.jpg", "description": "The Stairsteps perform \"O-o-h Child\" on Soul Train.\nThe lyrics tell us that \"things are gonna get easier\" for all of us, in times of strife. The song's uplifting message helped it to become popular among pop and rhythm and blues audiences when it was released in 1970.\n\nO-o-h Child\nLyrics:\nOoh child\nThings are gonna get easier\nOoh child\nThings'll get brighter\nOoh child\nThings are gonna get easier\nOoh child\nThings'll get brighter\nSome day, yeah\nWe'll put it together and we'll get it undone\nSome day\nWhen your head is much lighter\nSome day, yeah\nWe'll walk in the rays of a beautiful sun\nSome day\nWhen the world is much brighter\nOoh child\nThings are gonna be easier\nOoh child\nThings'll be brighter\nOoh child\nThings are gonna be easier\nOoh child\nThings'll be brighter\nSome day, yeah\nWe'll put it together and we'll get it undone\nSome day\nWhen your head is much lighter\nSome day, yeah\nWe'll walk in the rays of a beautiful sun\nSome day\nWhen the world is much brighter\nSome day, some day, some day, some day yeah\nWe'll put it together and we'll get it undone\nSome day\nWhen your head is much lighter\nSome day, yeah\nWe'll walk in the rays of a beautiful sun\nSome day\nWhen the world is much brighter\nOoh child\nThings are gonna get easier\nOoh child\nThings'll get brighter\nOoh child\nThings are gonna get easier\nOoh child\nThings'll get brighter\n(Right now)\nOh yeah\n(Right now)\nOh baby\n(Right now) and you just wait and see how things are gonna be\n(Right now) if you just wait and see how things are gonna be\n(Right now) if you just wait and wait and see\n\n------------------------------------------\n\nThe Five Stairsteps, known as \"The First Family of Soul\" were a Chicago soul group made up of five of Betty and Clarence Burke Sr.'s six children: Alohe Jean, Clarence Jr., James, Dennis, and Kenneth \"Keni\", and briefly, Cubie. They are best known for the 1970 song \"O-o-h Child\", listed at number 402 on Rolling Stone's 500 Greatest Songs of All Time.\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nAbout Our Nostalgic Memories:\nWe all come from different times and places, but there are commonalities, or threads, that bind us and bring us closer to one another.  Let us rejoice in the simple days of the past.  Our Nostalgic Memories is dedicated to remembering the best of times and the best of people.